According to Professor Sax the Public Trust Doctrine imposes the following restrictions on governmental authority :-
Three types of restrictions on governmental authority are often thought to be imposed by the public trust: first, the property subject to the trust must not only be used for a public purpose, but it must be held available for use by the general public;
second, the property may not be sold, even for a fair cash equivalent; and third the property must be maintained for particular types of uses.
